# Route-data backups written by Tools ▸ Alipiri AR ▸ Import KML Route — local recovery
# artifacts, not source. Deliberately outside Assets/ so they never ship inside the APK.
/Backups/

# Unity 6 il2cpp / burst backup dirs
# The leading `/[Bb]ackup*` form only matched folders literally starting with "Backup" —
# Unity names them "<ProductName>_BackUpThisFolder_...", so the real one (693 files of build
# output at the repo root) slipped through. Match the suffix instead.
/*[Bb]ackUpThisFolder_ButDontShipItWithYourGame/
/[Bb]ackup*ButDontShipItWithYourGame/
/*_BurstDebugInformation_DoNotShip/
/.utmp/

# Third-party installers — never source. Docs/ProtonVPN_v5.1.7_x64.exe is 127 MB, which also
# exceeds GitHub's 100 MB hard per-file limit and would reject the push outright.
*.exe
*.msi

# Local Excel export (regenerated at runtime, contains personal data)
Assets/login.xlsx
Assets/login.xlsx.meta

# Live Google Maps Tiles API key — restricted per Android package + SHA-1 in Cloud Console
# (see GoogleTileSession's class doc), but still not something to commit. Ship
# map_api_key.example.txt instead; each dev/CI machine drops its own real key in locally.
Assets/StreamingAssets/map_api_key.txt
Assets/StreamingAssets/map_api_key.txt.meta

# ARCore Extensions writes its Android/iOS Cloud Services API key into this file as plain JSON
# (Google.XR.ARCoreExtensions.Internal.ARCoreExtensionsProjectSettings._projectSettingsPath,
# verified against the actual package source in LocalPackages/) — unlike everywhere else Unity
# stores project config, this one file genuinely doesn't belong under version control. Unlike
# StreamingAssets, ProjectSettings/ is NOT excluded above (by design — TagManager.asset,
# ProjectSettings.asset etc. are meant to be tracked), so this needs its own explicit line or the
# next commit from anyone who's set an API key in the ARCore Extensions Inspector leaks it.
ProjectSettings/ARCoreExtensionsProjectSettings.json

*.exe
*.apk


*_BackUpThisFolder*
Builds/
Library/
Temp/
Logs/

